{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ec70e3f1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Empirical Example for Sensitivity Analysis: 401(k) Eligibility and Financial Wealth\n",
    "\n",
    "This is an adaptation of the replication package for Chernozhukov, Cinelli, Newey, Sharma and Syrgkanis,\n",
    "*Long Story Short: Omitted Variable Bias in Causal Machine Learning* \n",
    "\n",
    "The original replication package can be found __[here](https://dataverse.harvard.edu/dataset.xhtml?persistentId=doi:10.7910/DVN/VH6QHQ)__."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "170f2037",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-11T14:54:10.878737Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-11T14:54:10.877672Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-11T14:54:11.736717Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-11T14:54:11.736203Z"
    },
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install packages if needed\n",
    "repos <- c(CRAN = \"https://cloud.r-project.org\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if (!requireNamespace(\"remotes\", quietly = TRUE))   install.packages(\"remotes\", repos = repos)\n",
    "if (!requireNamespace(\"sensemakr\", quietly = TRUE)) install.packages(\"sensemakr\", repos = repos)\n",
    "if (!requireNamespace(\"ggplot2\", quietly = TRUE))   install.packages(\"ggplot2\", repos = repos)\n",
    "if (!requireNamespace(\"ranger\", quietly = TRUE))    install.packages(\"ranger\", repos = repos)\n",
    "if (!requireNamespace(\"dml.sensemakr\", quietly = TRUE)) {\n",
    "  remotes::install_github(\"carloscinelli/dml.sensemakr\", upgrade = \"never\")\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "267a6538",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-11T14:54:11.745657Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-11T14:54:11.738176Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-11T14:54:11.759105Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-11T14:54:11.758692Z"
    },
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "dml.sensemakr 0.2.2 \n",
      "sensemakr     0.1.6 \n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "suppressMessages({\n",
    "  library(sensemakr)       # attached first: we only need add_bound_to_contour()\n",
    "  library(dml.sensemakr)   # attached last:  keeps its methods for class \"dml\" unmasked\n",
    "  library(ggplot2)\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "options(scipen = 99)  \n",
    "\n",
    "# figure sizing inside the notebook\n",
    "options(repr.plot.width = 7, repr.plot.height = 6, repr.plot.res = 150)\n",
    "\n",
    "dir.create(\"figures\", showWarnings = FALSE)\n",
    "\n",
    "cat(\"dml.sensemakr\", as.character(packageVersion(\"dml.sensemakr\")), \"\\n\")\n",
    "cat(\"sensemakr    \", as.character(packageVersion(\"sensemakr\")), \"\\n\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a7079423",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setting\n",
    "\n",
    "The outcome $Y$ is net financial assets and the treatment $D$ is eligibility to enroll in a 401(k) plan. The observed covariates $X^o$ include income, age, education, family size, marital status, two-earner status, IRA participation, and home ownership. The identifying argument used in earlier work is that, after conditioning on these worker characteristics, eligibility is approximately as good as randomly assigned.\n",
    "\n",
    "However, the threat is that unobserved firm characteristics $A$ may affect both eligibility and financial assets, for example through employer matching policies. Conditional ignorability then holds given the full $X = (X^o, A)$, while the data identify only functions of the short regressor vector $W_s = (D, X^o)$. What we can estimate is the short parameter $\\theta_s$. The task is to bound its\n",
    "distance from the causal target $\\theta$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "641048b9",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-11T14:54:11.760854Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-11T14:54:11.760463Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-11T14:54:11.771931Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-11T14:54:11.771465Z"
    },
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "households: 9915   covariates: 8   eligible: 37.1% \n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "data(\"pension\")\n",
    "\n",
    "y <- pension$net_tfa   # Y: net total financial assets\n",
    "d <- pension$e401      # D: 401(k) eligibility\n",
    "\n",
    "# X^o: the observed worker characteristics\n",
    "x <- model.matrix(~ -1 + age + inc + educ + fsize + marr + twoearn + pira + hown,\n",
    "                  data = pension)\n",
    "\n",
    "cat(\"households:\", nrow(x), \"  covariates:\", ncol(x),\n",
    "    \"  eligible:\", sprintf(\"%.1f%%\", 100 * mean(d)), \"\\n\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5be9f408",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Short Estimates Under Conditional Ignorability\n",
    "\n",
    "### Partially Linear Model\n",
    "\n",
    "The first specification is the partially linear model,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$Y = \\theta_s D + f_s(X^o) + \\varepsilon, \\qquad \\mathrm{E}[\\varepsilon \\mid D, X^o] = 0,$$\n",
    "\n",
    "with the nuisance functions modeled by random forests, cross-fitted over five folds and repeated five times."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "f4dad1cf",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-11T14:54:11.773658Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-11T14:54:11.773277Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-11T14:54:38.547333Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-11T14:54:38.546902Z"
    },
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "\n",
       "Debiased Machine Learning\n",
       "\n",
       " Model: Partially Linear \n",
       " Cross-Fitting: 5 folds, 5 reps \n",
       " ML Method: outcome (yreg0:ranger, yreg1:ranger, R2 = 26.474%), treatment (ranger, R2 = 11.599%)\n",
       " Tuning: dirty \n",
       "\n",
       "Average Treatment Effect : \n",
       "\n",
       "    Estimate Std. Error t value          P(>|t|)    \n",
       "ate     9114       1323   6.888 0.00000000000567 ***\n",
       "---\n",
       "Signif. codes:  0 '***' 0.001 '**' 0.01 '*' 0.05 '.' 0.1 ' ' 1\n",
       "Note: DML estimates combined using the median method.\n",
       "\n",
       "Verbal interpretation of DML procedure:\n",
       "\n",
       "-- Average treatment effects were estimated using DML with 5-fold cross-fitting. In order to reduce the variance that stems from sample splitting, we repeated the procedure 5 times. Estimates are combined using the median as the final estimate, incorporating variation across experiments into the standard error as described in Chernozhukov et al. (2018). The outcome regression uses Random Forest from the R package ranger; the treatment regression uses Random Forest from the R package ranger."
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "set.seed(1)\n",
    "dml.401k.plm <- dml(y, d, x, model = \"plm\", cf.folds = 5, cf.reps = 5, verbose = FALSE)\n",
    "\n",
    "summary(dml.401k.plm)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "994cf0bc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Nonparametric Model, with Income Groups\n",
    "\n",
    "The second specification drops the additive structure. The short regression\n",
    "$g_s(W_s) = \\mathrm{E}[Y \\mid D, X^o]$ is left unrestricted and the target is the average contrast,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\theta_s = \\mathrm{E}\\big\\{g_s(1, X^o) - g_s(0, X^o)\\big\\},$$\n",
    "\n",
    "estimated with the same nuisance learners. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "c886bdf1",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-11T14:54:38.550249Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-11T14:54:38.549906Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-11T14:54:38.554742Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-11T14:54:38.554353Z"
    },
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# income quartiles\n",
    "g1 <- cut(x[, \"inc\"],\n",
    "          quantile(x[, \"inc\"], c(0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1), na.rm = TRUE),\n",
    "          labels = c(\"q1\", \"q2\", \"q3\", \"q4\"), include.lowest = TRUE)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "e281ccde",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-11T14:54:38.556283Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-11T14:54:38.555936Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-11T14:55:06.503086Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-11T14:55:06.502651Z"
    },
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "\n",
       "Debiased Machine Learning\n",
       "\n",
       " Model: Nonparametric \n",
       " Cross-Fitting: 5 folds, 5 reps \n",
       " ML Method: outcome (yreg0:ranger, yreg1:ranger, R2 = 25.572%), treatment (ranger, R2 = 11.48%)\n",
       " Tuning: dirty \n",
       "\n",
       "Average Treatment Effect : \n",
       "\n",
       "    Estimate Std. Error t value          P(>|t|)    \n",
       "ate     8198       1196   6.852 0.00000000000726 ***\n",
       "---\n",
       "Signif. codes:  0 '***' 0.001 '**' 0.01 '*' 0.05 '.' 0.1 ' ' 1\n",
       "\n",
       "Group Average Treatment Effect: \n",
       "\n",
       "         Estimate Std. Error t value       P(>|t|)    \n",
       "g.ate.q1   4646.2      794.2   5.850 0.00000000492 ***\n",
       "g.ate.q2   2729.4     1296.7   2.105      0.035305 *  \n",
       "g.ate.q3   6854.3     1838.0   3.729      0.000192 ***\n",
       "g.ate.q4  18406.6     4061.6   4.532 0.00000584674 ***\n",
       "---\n",
       "Signif. codes:  0 '***' 0.001 '**' 0.01 '*' 0.05 '.' 0.1 ' ' 1\n",
       "\n",
       "Note: DML estimates combined using the median method.\n",
       "\n",
       "Verbal interpretation of DML procedure:\n",
       "\n",
       "-- Average treatment effects were estimated using DML with 5-fold cross-fitting. In order to reduce the variance that stems from sample splitting, we repeated the procedure 5 times. Estimates are combined using the median as the final estimate, incorporating variation across experiments into the standard error as described in Chernozhukov et al. (2018). The outcome regression uses Random Forest from the R package ranger; the treatment regression uses Random Forest from the R package ranger."
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "set.seed(1)\n",
    "dml.401k.npm <- dml(y, d, x, groups = g1, model = \"npm\",\n",
    "                    cf.folds = 5, cf.reps = 5, verbose = FALSE)\n",
    "\n",
    "summary(dml.401k.npm)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ef3e8146",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Group Effects by Income Quartile\n",
    "\n",
    "Plotted against income quartile, with sampling confidence bounds under conditional ignorability,\n",
    "the pattern in the summary above is easier to read.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "5c41f860",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-11T14:55:06.505709Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-11T14:55:06.505362Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-11T14:55:06.510354Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-11T14:55:06.509927Z"
    },
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "group.names <- setdiff(names(coef(dml.401k.npm)), \"ate\")\n",
    "\n",
    "df  <- data.frame(groups = 1:4, estimate = coef(dml.401k.npm)[group.names])\n",
    "cis <- setNames(as.data.frame(confint(dml.401k.npm)[group.names, ]), c(\"lwr.ci\", \"upr.ci\"))\n",
    "df  <- cbind(df, cis)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "522bd397",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-11T14:55:06.511809Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-11T14:55:06.511512Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-11T14:55:06.689836Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-11T14:55:06.689403Z"
    },
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
