     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "rv.plm <- robustness_value(dml.401k.plm)\n",
    "rv.npm <- robustness_value(dml.401k.npm)\n",
    "\n",
    "cat(sprintf(\"RV_alpha  (alpha = 0.05, threshold theta = 0)\\n  partially linear : %.1f%%\\n  nonparametric    : %.1f%%\\n\",\n",
    "            100 * rv.plm[\"ate\"], 100 * rv.npm[\"ate\"]))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "99f710a6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## The Main Confounding Scenario\n",
    "\n",
    "The main scenario assumes that omitted firm characteristics explain as much outcome variation as the\n",
    "maximum employer match accumulated over three years, which implies approximately $C_Y^2 = 0.04$. On\n",
    "the treatment side it allows an additional 2.5 percentage points of eligibility variation beyond the\n",
    "observed controls, corresponding to $q_\\alpha \\approx 0.03$. We take $|\\rho| = 1$, the conservative\n",
    "case in which the two induced errors are perfectly aligned.\n",
    "\n",
    "What $q_\\alpha$ measures depends on the target: for the partially linear model it is the\n",
    "nonparametric partial $R^2$ of the treatment with the omitted covariates, and for the\n",
    "binary-treatment ATE a gain in average inverse-variance precision.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "8a03f2af",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.064135Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.063812Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.069566Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.069163Z"
    },
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cf.y <- 0.04   # C_Y^2\n",
    "cf.d <- 0.03   # q_alpha\n",
    "rho2 <- 1      # |rho| = 1\n",
    "\n",
    "bounds.plm <- dml_bounds(dml.401k.plm, cf.y = cf.y, cf.d = cf.d, rho2 = rho2)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "eb62473e",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.071060Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.070750Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.077621Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.077164Z"
    },
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "bounds.npm <- dml_bounds(dml.401k.npm, cf.y = cf.y, cf.d = cf.d, rho2 = rho2)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "b6c06ec7",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.079155Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.078850Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.090590Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.090101Z"
    },
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cb.plm <- confidence_bounds(dml.401k.plm, cf.y = cf.y, cf.d = cf.d, rho2 = rho2)\n",
    "cb.npm <- confidence_bounds(dml.401k.npm, cf.y = cf.y, cf.d = cf.d, rho2 = rho2)"
   ]
  },
  {
