     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "dollars <- function(v) formatC(round(v), format = \"d\", big.mark = \",\")\n",
    "\n",
    "row <- function(bounds, cb, label) {\n",
    "  b <- coef(bounds)[, \"ate\"]\n",
    "  data.frame(\n",
    "    Model              = label,\n",
    "    `Short ATE`        = dollars(b[\"theta.s\"]),\n",
    "    `Bias bound`       = dollars(b[\"bias.bound\"]),\n",
    "    `ATE bounds`       = sprintf(\"[%s, %s]\", dollars(b[\"theta.m\"]), dollars(b[\"theta.p\"])),\n",
    "    `95% conf. bounds` = sprintf(\"[%s, %s]\", dollars(cb[\"ate\", 1]), dollars(cb[\"ate\", 2])),\n",
    "    row.names = NULL,\n",
    "    check.names = FALSE\n",
    "  )\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "table2.3 <- rbind(row(bounds.plm, cb.plm, \"Partially linear\"),\n",
    "                  row(bounds.npm, cb.npm, \"Nonparametric\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "table2.3\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "89ff8ba9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Even granting an adversarially aligned confounder as strong as three years of maximum employer match,\n",
    "the lower confidence bound on the ATE remains positive in both specifications."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d6f07816",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Group Effects Under the Scenario\n",
    "\n",
    "The same groups again, now with the sensitivity bounds in red and the wider confidence bounds in\n",
    "blue.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "9b0a3776",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.104074Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.103749Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.236165Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.235716Z"
    },
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "plot without title"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {
      "image/png": {
       "height": 450,
       "width": 525
      }
     },
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "bds  <- setNames(as.data.frame(confidence_bounds(dml.401k.npm, cf.y = cf.y, cf.d = cf.d, level = 0)),\n",
    "                 c(\"lwr.bound\", \"upr.bound\"))\n",
    "cbds <- setNames(as.data.frame(confidence_bounds(dml.401k.npm, cf.y = cf.y, cf.d = cf.d, level = 0.95)),\n",
    "                 c(\"lwr.cbound\", \"upr.cbound\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "df2 <- cbind(df, bds[-1, ], cbds[-1, ])\n",
    "\n",
    "p2 <- ggplot(df2, aes(x = groups, y = estimate)) +\n",
    "  geom_line() +\n",
    "  geom_ribbon(aes(ymin = lwr.bound,  ymax = upr.bound),  alpha = 0.1, col = \"red\",  fill = \"red\") +\n",
    "  geom_ribbon(aes(ymin = lwr.cbound, ymax = upr.cbound), alpha = 0.1, col = \"blue\", fill = \"blue\") +\n",
    "  theme_bw() +\n",
    "  xlab(\"Income Groups by Quartiles\") +\n",
    "  ylab(\"ATE\") +\n",
    "  ggtitle(\"With unobserved confounding\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ggsave(\"figures/401K-groups-confounding.pdf\", p2, width = 4.5, height = 4.5)\n",
    "p2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0ba2ae32",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The posited confounding scenario substantially widens the range of plausible effects but leaves most of the adjusted region positive. Only the second quartile has a small excursion below zero."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "752bb83c",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
