    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "p_combined <- ggplot(df2, aes(x = groups, y = estimate)) +\n",
    "  geom_ribbon(aes(ymin = lwr.cbound, ymax = upr.cbound), fill = \"blue\", alpha = 0.03, color = NA) +\n",
    "  geom_ribbon(aes(ymin = lwr.bound,  ymax = upr.bound),  fill = \"blue\", alpha = 0.12, color = NA) +\n",
    "  geom_line(color = \"black\") +\n",
    "  geom_line(aes(y = lwr.ci),    color = \"black\", linetype = \"dashed\") +\n",
    "  geom_line(aes(y = upr.ci),    color = \"black\", linetype = \"dashed\") +\n",
    "  geom_line(aes(y = lwr.bound), color = \"blue\") +\n",
    "  geom_line(aes(y = upr.bound), color = \"blue\") +\n",
    "  geom_line(aes(y = lwr.cbound), color = \"blue\", linetype = \"dashed\") +\n",
    "  geom_line(aes(y = upr.cbound), color = \"blue\", linetype = \"dashed\") +\n",
    "  theme_bw() +\n",
    "  theme(plot.title = element_text(hjust = 0.5)) +\n",
    "  xlab(\"Income Groups by Quartiles\") +\n",
    "  ylab(\"ATE\") +\n",
    "  ggtitle(\"Confidence and Sensitivity Bounds\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ggsave(\"figures/401k-groups-sensitivity-combined.pdf\", p_combined, width = 4.5, height = 4.5)\n",
    "p_combined\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "651c1a8d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Benchmarking\n",
    "\n",
    "Rather than posit $C_Y$ and $C_D$ in the abstract, we can calibrate them against a covariate we do observe. The procedure is as follows: drop the covariate from $X^o$, refit, and read off the gains it supplied. Latent confounding is then described relative to the chosen benchmarking variable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "b4a7321f",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.238274Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-11T14:55:07.237941Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-11T14:56:25.265989Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-11T14:56:25.265444Z"
    },
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "set.seed(2)\n",
    "invisible(capture.output(\n",
    "  bench.plm <- dml_benchmark(dml.401k.plm,\n",
    "                             benchmark_covariates = c(\"inc\", \"pira\", \"twoearn\"))\n",
    "))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "085c0865",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`gain.Y` is the implied $C_Y^2$ and `gain.D` the implied $q_\\alpha$. Income is a strong predictor of both eligibility and financial assets; IRA participation and two-earner status are considerably weaker.\n",
    "\n",
    "The `rho` column records the alignment each covariate actually exhibits. None is anywhere near $\\pm 1$, which is a first indication of how conservative the worst-case analysis is.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "9837c2cf",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-11T14:56:25.271430Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-11T14:56:25.271070Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-11T14:56:25.284321Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-11T14:56:25.283894Z"
    },
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/html": [
       "<table class=\"dataframe\">\n",
       "<caption>A matrix: 3 × 3 of type dbl</caption>\n",
       "<thead>\n",
       "\t<tr><th></th><th scope=col>gain.Y</th><th scope=col>gain.D</th><th scope=col>rho</th></tr>\n",
       "</thead>\n",
       "<tbody>\n",
       "\t<tr><th scope=row>inc</th><td>0.1366</td><td>0.0502</td><td>-0.3372</td></tr>\n",
       "\t<tr><th scope=row>pira</th><td>0.0487</td><td>0.0081</td><td>-0.1317</td></tr>\n",
       "\t<tr><th scope=row>twoearn</th><td>0.0399</td><td>0.0112</td><td> 0.2589</td></tr>\n",
       "</tbody>\n",
       "</table>\n"
      ],
      "text/latex": [
       "A matrix: 3 × 3 of type dbl\n",
       "\\begin{tabular}{r|lll}\n",
       "  & gain.Y & gain.D & rho\\\\\n",
